(823874, 91379, 23300, '<td valign="top">I really like the overall golden colour. The focus seems a little too soft. I like the composition. I think a border would add to this image.</td>', 'I really like the overall golden colour. The focus seems a little too soft. I like the composition. I think a border would add to this image.', '2004-07-24 03:53:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(823875, 92648, 23300, '<td valign="top">The bright colours make a strong impact. Even the harsh lighting ads to the dynamics of this image. I would have cropped it to include only the three bags at the front and sharpened the focus a little.</td>', 'The bright colours make a strong impact. Even the harsh lighting ads to the dynamics of this image. I would have cropped it to include only the three bags at the front and sharpened the focus a little.', '2004-07-24 03:55:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(823880, 92579, 23300, '<td valign="top">I like the colour combinations in this image. The light is a bit flat for my liking. I think a lower light could have added some more shadows and detail into the little white chocolates. I think the central composition works. I would have added a little more room all round and added a border.</td>', 'I like the colour combinations in this image. The light is a bit flat for my liking. I think a lower light could have added some more shadows and detail into the little white chocolates. I think the central composition works. I would have added a little more room all round and added a border.', '2004-07-24 04:00:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(823886, 92056, 23300, '<td valign="top">This image has a sort of fairytale feel about it. The colours work really well. I would have opened up the depth of field so that everything was in focus. I would also suggest that cropping it to include the whole hot chocolate bottle would help to balance the composition. I think the foreground elements work really well. You''ve achieved a "random balance" in the placement and colouring of these elements.</td>', 'This image has a sort of fairytale feel about it. The colours work really well. I would have opened up the depth of field so that everything was in focus. I would also suggest that cropping it to include the whole hot chocolate bottle would help to balance the composition. I think the foreground elements work really well. You''ve achieved a "random balance" in the placement and colouring of these elements.', '2004-07-24 04:06:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(823887, 92450, 20029, '<td valign="top">This is my blue ribbon picture for this challenge! Hope you win. its a little blown out on the left but that doesn''t really take much away from this picture. It diserves to be hung in a museum! (yes, I am serious) Hope you win and good luck!</td>', 'This is my blue ribbon picture for this challenge! Hope you win. its a little blown out on the left but that doesn''t really take much away from this picture. It diserves to be hung in a museum! (yes, I am serious) Hope you win and good luck!', '2004-07-24 04:06:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(823894, 91994, 23300, '<td valign="top">Good idea. I think a few simple things could really improve this image. A neater surface for the subject like a board or table top that wouldn''t get ripples in it. I think if the image included more of the hand and a bit of the wrist it would balance the composition more. It looks like you used a flash making the lighting a bit sharp. I think a light setup to one side would create some interesting shadows across the surface and would reduce the white dots on the chocolates. I also would have focused the camera on the chocolates at the front of the shot. The way you placed the chocolates works for me creating a nice "random balance."</td>', 'Good idea. I think a few simple things could really improve this image. A neater surface for the subject like a board or table top that wouldn''t get ripples in it. I think if the image included more of the hand and a bit of the wrist it would balance the composition more. It looks like you used a flash making the lighting a bit sharp. I think a light setup to one side would create some interesting shadows across the surface and would reduce the white dots on the chocolates. I also would have focused the camera on the chocolates at the front of the shot. The way you placed the chocolates works for me creating a nice "random balance."', '2004-07-24 04:13:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(823896, 92553, 24582, '<td valign="top">Very Cool............actually I should say very "Hot"</td>', 'Very Cool............actually I should say very "Hot"', '2004-07-24 04:14:47.000000', NULL, 1),
