(828695, 92691, 23203, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments folks. Original photograph had mnm''s and lindt on each side, but I had to crop pretty tight because the paper boundary showed.<br/> <br/>It was a last 3min entry, so couldnt retake the shot.<br/>Sure wish I had known about neatimage earlier.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments folks. Original photograph had mnm''s and lindt on each side, but I had to crop pretty tight because the paper boundary showed. It was a last 3min entry, so couldnt retake the shot.Sure wish I had known about neatimage earlier.', '2004-07-28 01:12:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(828697, 92377, 3649, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone who commented. This was an education, for sure... The work seems to have paid off! I couldn''t figure out what half the reflections were. The one on the left of the shaker is a 5-in-1 reflector on the soft gold side.<br/> <br/>I wish I had had some instant cocoa for the rim (as it should be served, anyway) but this was a mix of natural sugar and cocoa powder - much too "dirty". The lighting on the main subject really didn''t "pop" for me and I almost submitted a different shot entirely.<br/> <br/>Thanks again.</td>', 'Thanks to everyone who commented. This was an education, for sure... The work seems to have paid off! I couldn''t figure out what half the reflections were. The one on the left of the shaker is a 5-in-1 reflector on the soft gold side. I wish I had had some instant cocoa for the rim (as it should be served, anyway) but this was a mix of natural sugar and cocoa powder - much too "dirty". The lighting on the main subject really didn''t "pop" for me and I almost submitted a different shot entirely. Thanks again.', '2004-07-28 01:12:46.000000', NULL, 0),
