(832206, 91771, 12640, '<td valign="top">I also took a picture of a chocolate-dipped strawberry, but wasn''t satisfied with the results. So therefore, I didn''t enter it into the challenge. But this one truly deserves the ribbon it won!!  Good job! Very appetizing indeed!!<br/> <br/>Lisa</td>', 'I also took a picture of a chocolate-dipped strawberry, but wasn''t satisfied with the results. So therefore, I didn''t enter it into the challenge. But this one truly deserves the ribbon it won!!  Good job! Very appetizing indeed!! Lisa', '2004-07-29 16:06:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(832213, 92636, 8860, '<td valign="top"><b>Hello from the Critique Club!</b> <br/>......................................................<br/> <br/>Well, that''s certainly a hands-on approach to the packaging.<br/> <br/>I like this idea, but I find that there is too little context to suggest what is inside other than simply reading the label. Had this been a box with form and shot at an angle - maybe even half unwrapped - perhaps it would have been communicated better without relying on the wording and title.<br/> <br/>The cropping is tight horizontally, making for an awkward format.<br/> <br/>This is an image which, although fitting the challenge, may not endure well outside of the competition. You may find it useful to consider ''notonline''s'' comment and endeavour to produce even challenge photos that could grace yours (or other people''s) walls.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Jon</td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club! ...................................................... Well, that''s certainly a hands-on approach to the packaging. I like this idea, but I find that there is too little context to suggest what is inside other than simply reading the label. Had this been a box with form and shot at an angle - maybe even half unwrapped - perhaps it would have been communicated better without relying on the wording and title. The cropping is tight horizontally, making for an awkward format. This is an image which, although fitting the challenge, may not endure well outside of the competition. You may find it useful to consider ''notonline''s'' comment and endeavour to produce even challenge photos that could grace yours (or other people''s) walls. CheersJon', '2004-07-29 16:09:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(832231, 92585, 8860, '<td valign="top"><b>Hello from the Critique Club!</b> <br/>......................................................<br/> <br/>A yummy treat indeed - which means you''ve got this right in the main.<br/> <br/>Your lighting, focus and subject are superb, with the exception of the arrangement of the cake which does look messy (not enough to put me off however!). You have a slight green tinge on top of the cake which is a little off-putting, despite probably being a reflection of something natural. The crop is too tight at the top and too wide lower down, but otherwise it is a good composition. Exposure is also very well spread.<br/> <br/>Hope you enjoyed eating it!<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Jon</td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club! ...................................................... A yummy treat indeed - which means you''ve got this right in the main. Your lighting, focus and subject are superb, with the exception of the arrangement of the cake which does look messy (not enough to put me off however!). You have a slight green tinge on top of the cake which is a little off-putting, despite probably being a reflection of something natural. The crop is too tight at the top and too wide lower down, but otherwise it is a good composition. Exposure is also very well spread. Hope you enjoyed eating it! CheersJon', '2004-07-29 16:22:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(832246, 92519, 22748, '<td valign="top">Hmmm, thought I had commented on this during the challenge. I really like this one. I don''t mind the shallow DOF, it''s kind of nice, but I don''t know about the choice of focal point. Either a deeper DOF, or a focal point at the very bottom of the frame would be interesting to compare. This kind of blurry-&gt;sharp-&gt;blurry shallow DOF sometimes doesn''t feel "right" to me, though I usually like shallow DOF. Good shot though.<br/> <br/>So you used vegetable oil, but were the chips also actually melting? I''m thinking maybe not, after looking really close.</td>', 'Hmmm, thought I had commented on this during the challenge. I really like this one. I don''t mind the shallow DOF, it''s kind of nice, but I don''t know about the choice of focal point. Either a deeper DOF, or a focal point at the very bottom of the frame would be interesting to compare. This kind of blurry->sharp->blurry shallow DOF sometimes doesn''t feel "right" to me, though I usually like shallow DOF. Good shot though. So you used vegetable oil, but were the chips also actually melting? I''m thinking maybe not, after looking really close.', '2004-07-29 16:39:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(832891, 92642, 12252, '<td valign="top">I just wanted to thank all who commented on my photo. This was my best finish yet (by score, not placement). I got so many wonderful comments from so many people who I highly respect as photographers. For those of you who took the time after the challenge to post a comment, a special thanks as well. I just happened to come back to my picture tonight not expecting ANY after challenge comments, only to find four more. Very rewarding. Again, my thanks!</td>', 'I just wanted to thank all who commented on my photo. This was my best finish yet (by score, not placement). I got so many wonderful comments from so many people who I highly respect as photographers. For those of you who took the time after the challenge to post a comment, a special thanks as well. I just happened to come back to my picture tonight not expecting ANY after challenge comments, only to find four more. Very rewarding. Again, my thanks!', '2004-07-30 01:11:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(832962, 92667, 15511, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by the_Seeker:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice balance.  Too much reflection.  I like how the background is seamless however the texture comes off  like it''s digital noise to me. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This comment from below was correct. All the "artifacts" and "digital noise" was actually the texture of the white plastic cutting board that the chocolates were placed on. I''ve learned that it was not a suitable platform. Thanks to the rest of ya for the constructive criticism.</td>', 'Originally posted by the_Seeker: Nice balance.  Too much reflection.  I like how the background is seamless however the texture comes off  like it''s digital noise to me.   This comment from below was correct. All the "artifacts" and "digital noise" was actually the texture of the white plastic cutting board that the chocolates were placed on. I''ve learned that it was not a suitable platform. Thanks to the rest of ya for the constructive criticism.', '2004-07-30 03:58:44.000000', NULL, 0),
