(3371444, 92278, 70375, '<td valign="top">Okay, I was loving the photo until I saw that you SQUISHED the spider!!!! :(  BW''s are actually really really good pest control and are not lethal, poisionous, but not lethal. The only documented case of a BW killing a human was a 2 year old that was bitten MANY times by MANY spiders. I let one live in my basement for over a year :)  We had no bugs or other spiders during that time... she eventually moved out.<br/> <br/>This is a great photo! I cannot believe you captured this :) Tiny question for you (feel free to PM me the answer): Where is the red spot off her back? did you PP it out or is she turned so you cannot see it?? I admire your bravery for this too LOL :)</td>', 'Okay, I was loving the photo until I saw that you SQUISHED the spider!!!! :(  BW''s are actually really really good pest control and are not lethal, poisionous, but not lethal. The only documented case of a BW killing a human was a 2 year old that was bitten MANY times by MANY spiders. I let one live in my basement for over a year :)  We had no bugs or other spiders during that time... she eventually moved out. This is a great photo! I cannot believe you captured this :) Tiny question for you (feel free to PM me the answer): Where is the red spot off her back? did you PP it out or is she turned so you cannot see it?? I admire your bravery for this too LOL :)', '2007-02-15 23:51:21.000000', NULL, 0),
